          "section:Best Practices"
        ],
        "exercise": "safe-message",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "multi-catch-twr",
        "says": "Multi-catch and try-with-resources reduce duplicated handlers and keep exceptions from close().",
        "basis": [
          "section:Relevant Java Features"
        ],
        "exercise": null,
        "reason": "both are taught and practised in the try-catch module this page cites as background"
      },
      {
        "id": "no-flow-control",
        "says": "Exceptions are for exceptional conditions, not for ending a loop or signalling an ordinary outcome.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Common Pitfalls and How to Avoid Them"
        ],
        "exercise": "quiz",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "no-secrets",
        "says": "Exception messages reach logs, so they never hold passwords, tokens or full card numbers.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Common Pitfalls and How to Avoid Them"
        ],
        "exercise": "safe-message",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "no-swallowing",
        "says": "An empty catch block hides a failure; handle it, rethrow it, or at least log it.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Common Pitfalls and How to Avoid Them"
        ],
        "exercise": "import-once",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "reuse-standard",
        "says": "Standard exceptions such as IllegalArgumentException and IllegalStateException are reused when they describe the error.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Key Points to Remember",
          "example:12-custom-exception/README_3.2.3.md:3"
        ],
        "exercise": "seat-map",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "shallow-hierarchy",
        "says": "A shallow hierarchy, one base exception per module with a few subclasses, is easier to use than one class per message.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Common Pitfalls and How to Avoid Them",
          "section:Best Practices"
        ],
        "exercise": null,
        "reason": "a design judgement about a whole code base that no single practice can observe; 3.2.1's payment-describe practises a small domain family"
      },
      {
        "id": "throw-early-catch-late",
        "says": "Throw early where the input is checked, catch late where the caller can act.",
        "basis": [
          "section:Best Practices"
        ],
        "exercise": "import-once",
        "reason": null
      },
      {
        "id": "translate-with-cause",
        "says": "A layer translates a lower-level exception into its own, keeping the original as the cause.",
